    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Programme charter \u2014 burden-aware three-input logic in E. coli"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Directive \u2014 Fix the scientific question, the success criteria, and the stop conditions before any cloning."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Question"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Can a three-input transcriptional AND gate be operated in E. coli MG1655 across a full batch growth curve without the host burden collapsing its dynamic range?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Two-input gates are routine. The failure mode we care about appears at three inputs, where the summed expression load competes with growth and the gate output becomes a function of physiology rather than of its inputs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Success criteria"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ON/OFF ratio at least 20-fold at mid-exponential phase for all eight input states."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "That ratio retains at least 60 percent of its mid-exponential value at the onset of stationary phase."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Specific growth rate of the fully induced state within 20 percent of the empty-vector control."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stop conditions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If the two-input precursor cannot clear 20-fold, the three-input build is not attempted. Adding an input cannot repair a gate that is already marginal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If burden mitigation costs more than half the dynamic range, the architecture is rejected rather than tuned further."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
